id: 11
hanzi: 影子
pinyin: yǐng zi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: shadow; reflection; trace; glimpse
  es: sombra; reflejo; rastro; silueta

senses[3]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | shadow cast by an opaque object blocking light rays | sombra proyectada por un cuerpo al interceptar la luz | 树的影子 (shadow of the tree)
  2 | Noun | Standard | reflection or image cast in water, glass, or mirrors | reflejo o imagen proyectada en agua, espejos o superficies | 水中的影子 (reflection in the water)
  3 | Noun | Colloquial | faint trace, vague impression, or indication of something | indicio; rastro; señal remota o vaga | 连个影子都没有 (not a trace to be seen)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 除夕夜的月光洒在庭院里，地上映照出积雪和老树交错的影子，孩子们在院中欢快地嬉戏。 | Chúxī yè de yuèguāng sǎ zài tíngyuàn lǐ, dìshang yìngzhào chū jīxuě hé lǎoshù jiāocuò de yǐngzi, háizimen zài yuàn zhōng huānkuài de xīxì. | On New Year's Eve, moonlight spilled over the courtyard, casting intertwined shadows of old trees and snow on the ground as children played happily. | En la nochevieja, la luz de la luna bañaba el patio, proyectando sombras entrelazadas de nieve y viejos árboles mientras los niños jugaban alegremente.
  #2 | 在这份宏观经济调查报告中，我们不仅要分析表面的统计数据，更要看清潜藏在数字背后的结构性危机影子。 | Zài zhè fèn hóngguān jīngjì diàochá bàogào zhōng, wǒmen bùjǐn yào fēnxī biǎomiàn de tǒngjì shùjù, gèng yào kànqīng qiáncáng zài shùzì bèihòu de jiégòuxìng wēijī yǐngzi. | In this macroeconomic investigation report, we must not only analyze superficial statistical figures, but also clearly discern the looming shadow of structural crisis lurking behind the numbers. | En este informe de investigación macroeconómica, no solo debemos analizar los datos estadísticos superficiales, sino también distinguir con claridad la sombra de la crisis estructural que se oculta tras las cifras.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  留下影子 | leave a shadow; cast an impression
  阳光下的影子 | shadow under the sunlight
  毫无影子 | without a trace; not a sign of
  身影 | silhouette; figure
  捕捉影子 | capture a reflection or shadow
  影子的轮廓 | outline of a shadow

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  捕风捉影 | bǔ fēng zhuō yǐng | chase the wind and clutch at shadows; make groundless accusations
  形影不离 | xíng yǐng bù lí | inseparable as body and shadow; closely attached
  顾影自怜 | gù yǐng zì lián | look at one's own shadow and lament; wallow in self-pity
  立竿见影 | lì gān jiàn yǐng | set up a pole and see its shadow immediately; produce instant results

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  影 | yǐng | shadow; reflection; movie; image | sombra; reflejo; imagen; película | 彡 | bristle / light rays / shading | 日 (sun/light) + 彡 (rays/shading) | 京 (jīng, tall pavilion / phonetic) | 15 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound. Combines 景 (bright scenery under the sun 日 + 京) with 彡 (shading hair-lines/rays), portraying light creating silhouettes and shadows. | Bright sunlight (日) beams upon a magnificent city tower (京), casting long feathered brushstroke rays (彡) across the plaza floor to create a shadow. | La luz del sol (日) brilla sobre una gran torre (京), proyectando finas líneas de sombra (彡) en el suelo como pinceladas de plumaje. | 214 | AMHHH | 影
  子 | zi | noun suffix; offspring; seed | sufijo nominal; hijo; semilla | 子 | child / offspring | 子 (infant with head and swaddled limbs) | "" | 3 | 独体字 | Ancient pictograph of a newborn baby with head, arms open, and swaddled body, serving widely in modern vernacular Mandarin as a neutral-tone nominalizing suffix. | A tiny child (子) with outstretched arms, serving as a light suffix attached to concrete nouns to denote everyday tangible objects. | Un pequeño niño (子) con los brazos abiertos, que sirve como sufijo ligero para otorgar carácter tangible a sustantivos cotidianos. | 214 | ND | 子

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: When bright sunbeams create a silhouette (影), a tiny suffix (子) turns it into the tangible shadow (影子) cast beside you.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Cuando los rayos del sol dibujan una silueta (影), el sufijo nominal (子) forma la sombra (影子) perceptible que te acompaña.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical Chinese philosophy and literature, 影 (shadow) symbolizes the ephemeral nature of worldly appearances and the constant companion of solitary existence (as in Li Bai's famous poem 对影成三人, 'facing my shadow makes three of us'). The nominal suffix 子 softens the monosyllable into the common spoken noun 影子.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Low dipping 3rd tone 'yǐng' (214) followed by neutral tone 'zi' (2). The first syllable exhibits full dipping contour when isolated, but in fluent speech before the neutral tone, it maintains a low dip (21) while 'zi' is pronounced lightly and briefly at a low pitch.

