    晃 | huàng | sway; flash; dazzle
    照 | zhào | illuminate; reflect; photograph

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 影子 designates the actual physical dark area or optical reflection cast by an object blocking light, or figuratively a faint trace or looming threat.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 影子 vs. 身影 | shēnyǐng | 影子 denotes the optical silhouette cast by an obstruction of light or an inanimate object's shadow, whereas 身影 specifically refers to the visible posture, silhouette, or figure of a human body in motion or standing.
    2 | 影子 vs. 倒影 | dàoyǐng | 影子 refers to any cast shadow or optical profile on ground or walls, whereas 倒影 specifically designates an inverted optical reflection mirrored upside-down on a body of water or reflective polished surface.
    3 | 影子 vs. 迹象 | jìxiàng | 影子 figuratively denotes the lingering aura, ghost, or faint trace of an issue (e.g. 摆脱过去的影子), whereas 迹象 refers to objective empirical signs, clues, or indicators pointing to a future trend or past event (e.g. 经济复苏的迹象).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 月光下的长街寂静无声，路灯将行人的影子拉得很长。我们总在夜色里追寻前方的微光，却常常忽略了身后默默跟随的影子。它如同一面无言的镜子，映照着生命旅途中的孤独与坚定。 | Yuèguāng xià de chángjiē jìjìng wúshēng, lùdēng jiāng xíngrén de yǐngzi lā de hěn cháng. Wǒmen zǒng zài yèsè lǐ zhuīxún qiánfāng de wēiguāng, què chángcháng hūlüè le shēnhòu mòmò gēnsuí de yǐngzi. Tā rútóng yí miàn wúyán de jìngzi, yìngzhào zhe shēngmìng lǚtú zhōng de gūdú yǔ jiāndìng. | Under the moonlight, the long street is tranquil and silent, while street lamps stretch the shadows of pedestrians very long. We always seek the faint light ahead in the night, yet often overlook the shadow silently following behind us. Like a mute mirror, it reflects the loneliness and steadfast resolve throughout life's journey. | Bajo la luna, la larga calle está en silencio sepulcral, mientras las farolas estiran las sombras de los transeúntes. Solemos perseguir la tenue luz del camino en la noche, descuidando a menudo la sombra que nos sigue en silencio. Como un espejo mudo, refleja la soledad y la firmeza a lo largo del viaje de la vida.
  #2 | 在现代城市规划与高层建筑设计中，建筑影子对公共空间的遮挡已成为环境评估的关键指标。合理的楼间距不仅能消除深沉影子的压迫感，还能确保冬季充足的自然采光，让绿色低碳理念融入日常。 | Zài xiàndài chéngshì guīhuà yǔ gāocéng jiànzhù shèjì zhōng, jiànzhù yǐngzi duì gōnggòng kōngjiān de zhēdǎng yǐ chéngwéi huánjìng pínggū de guānjiàn zhǐbiāo. Hélǐ de lóujiānjù bùjǐn néng xiāochú shēnchén yǐngzi de yāpògǎn, hái néng quèbǎo dōngjì chōngzú de zìrán cǎiguāng, ràng lǜsè dītàn lǐniàn róngrù rìcháng. | In modern urban planning and high-rise architecture design, the obstruction of public spaces by building shadows has become a crucial environmental assessment index. Reasonable building spacing not only eliminates oppressive deep shadows, but also guarantees ample natural sunlight in winter, integrating green low-carbon concepts into daily life. | En el urbanismo moderno y el diseño de rascacielos, la obstrucción del espacio público por la sombra de los edificios es un índice clave de evaluación ambiental. Una distancia adecuada entre edificios mitiga la opresión de sombras densas y asegura iluminación natural en invierno, integrando el concepto ecológico en lo cotidiano.
